1
00:00:05,400 --> 00:00:12,433
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:40,833
[SCREAMING IN PAIN]

3
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:43,333
[TIRES SCREECHING]

4
00:00:45,333 --> 00:00:46,767
- [ENGINE REVVING]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

5
00:00:55,800 --> 00:00:57,333
[TIRES SCREECH]

6
00:00:58,100 --> 00:00:59,767
[ENGINES REVVING]

7
00:00:59,867 --> 00:01:01,000
[TRUCK HORN BLARES]

8
00:01:01,133 --> 00:01:02,267
[LOUD CRASH]

9
00:01:02,433 --> 00:01:04,600
[TIRES SCREECHING]

10
00:01:06,033 --> 00:01:07,800
- Stop!
- [GUNSHOTS]

11
00:01:10,333 --> 00:01:12,200
[FIREWORKS EXPLODING]

12
00:01:13,333 --> 00:01:17,300
[METAL RODS CLANGING]

13
00:01:17,400 --> 00:01:19,467
- [ENGINE REVVING]
- [BUS HORN HONKS]

14
00:01:20,333 --> 00:01:22,267
[GLASS SHATTERING]

15
00:01:22,367 --> 00:01:25,200
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [LOUD CRASH]

16
00:01:25,733 --> 00:01:28,367
[ENGINE REVVING]

17
00:01:29,967 --> 00:01:31,767
[TIRES SCREECHING]

18
00:01:32,467 --> 00:01:35,467
[TIRES SCREECHING]

19
00:01:35,567 --> 00:01:36,633
[GUNSHOTS]

20
00:01:36,800 --> 00:01:38,033
[TIRES SCREECHING]

21
00:01:38,167 --> 00:01:39,267
- [TRUCK HORN HONKS]
- [LOUD CRASH]

22
00:01:39,367 --> 00:01:42,500
[TIRES SCREECHING]

23
00:01:45,700 --> 00:01:49,333
<i>You have so many transactions
you need to close today.</i>

24
00:01:49,500 --> 00:01:53,333
<i>Mariano and I worked hard
to grow all of this.</i>

25
00:01:53,433 --> 00:01:55,000
<i> So, I want you...</i>

26
00:01:55,167 --> 00:01:57,067
<i> to prioritize the business!</i>

27
00:01:57,200 --> 00:02:00,233
<i>Django, it's rumored that Gabo
took Binoy, Tolits, and Daboy.</i>

28
00:02:00,367 --> 00:02:01,533
They're part oh his circle now!

29
00:02:01,700 --> 00:02:05,300
<i>You should stop Gabo
before he becomes well-known.</i>

30
00:02:05,400 --> 00:02:06,800
<i>We'll strengthen
our forces, Pa.</i>

31
00:02:06,900 --> 00:02:09,800
<i>I'll make sure
he won't make a move.</i>

32
00:02:09,900 --> 00:02:12,833
<i>Alpha one, on-site.
What's your status?</i>

33
00:02:12,933 --> 00:02:14,300
<i> Alpha two, in position.</i>

34
00:02:14,433 --> 00:02:15,533
<i>Positive.
Mr. Chan is inside.</i>

35
00:02:15,700 --> 00:02:17,867
<i>We called in
as potential buyers.</i>

36
00:02:17,967 --> 00:02:20,033
<i>The vendor said she
will ask her boss first.</i>

37
00:02:20,200 --> 00:02:22,267
<i>What if we split
into two groups?</i>

38
00:02:22,400 --> 00:02:23,833
<i>Let's come up
with our own gimmick</i>

39
00:02:23,933 --> 00:02:25,867
<i>so we don't look
stupid standing here.</i>

40
00:02:25,967 --> 00:02:27,000
<i> No, this is what we'll do.</i>

41
00:02:29,400 --> 00:02:30,333
<i> We're on the other side.</i>

42
00:02:30,433 --> 00:02:31,500
Won't we have a hard time
with this, ma'am?

43
00:02:31,600 --> 00:02:33,367
<i>The case we are handling
is too heavy.</i>

44
00:02:33,533 --> 00:02:35,867
<i>We need to follow him,
then we'll entrap him there.</i>

45
00:02:36,033 --> 00:02:38,100
- [CHEERING, APPLAUDING]
- Hey, what's going on?

46
00:02:38,233 --> 00:02:40,100
<i>- Have you seen him?
- No.</i>

47
00:02:40,233 --> 00:02:41,867
<i> We need to catch Tiger.</i>

48
00:02:42,033 --> 00:02:43,367
<i> We need to follow Mr. Chan</i>

49
00:02:43,467 --> 00:02:46,267
<i>because he's going
to take us to Tiger.</i>

50
00:02:47,467 --> 00:02:51,267
<i>The people's way
of thinking is--</i>

51
00:02:51,433 --> 00:02:53,400
[ARNEL] Let's go.
Let's go back to the office.

52
00:02:53,567 --> 00:02:56,233
- Let's go. [GROANS]
- in Ginintuang Lupa.

53
00:02:56,333 --> 00:02:58,400
Hey, stop looking
at your phone. Let's go.

54
00:02:58,567 --> 00:03:00,033
[DOOR SLIDES, CLOSES]

55
00:03:00,133 --> 00:03:01,633
What are you watching?

56
00:03:01,767 --> 00:03:04,400
Sir, isn't this
what we're covering?

57
00:03:04,567 --> 00:03:06,467
- Here. Take a look.
- it's for Ginintuang Lupa.

58
00:03:06,600 --> 00:03:08,733
<i>Not only do they lack
common sense,</i>

59
00:03:08,833 --> 00:03:11,567
<i>they also have
no breeding!</i>

60
00:03:12,233 --> 00:03:13,300
<i> Can you believe</i>

61
00:03:13,433 --> 00:03:14,733
<i> that when we went there</i>

62
00:03:14,900 --> 00:03:18,633
<i>with the owner
of Ginintuang Lupa,</i>

63
00:03:18,767 --> 00:03:21,400
<i>we were beaten
and pelted with stones?</i>

64
00:03:21,533 --> 00:03:25,967
<i>Don't they know that
he is a retired general!</i>

65
00:03:26,367 --> 00:03:28,667
<i> A little respect, please.</i>

66
00:03:29,133 --> 00:03:30,333
- Wow.
- Hey.

67
00:03:30,467 --> 00:03:34,633
<i> People of Ginintuang Lupa,</i>

68
00:03:34,800 --> 00:03:38,100
<i>- that land isn't yours!
- Oli.</i>

69
00:03:38,267 --> 00:03:42,433
Find out who that general is
who owns Ginintuang Lupa.

70
00:03:42,800 --> 00:03:44,500
- [ARNEL] Let's go.
- [ENGINE HUMMS]

71
00:03:46,467 --> 00:03:47,300
[ESTRELLA] Ma'am.

72
00:03:47,867 --> 00:03:48,600
[DOOR SLAMS]

73
00:03:48,767 --> 00:03:50,400
Watch this.

74
00:03:52,300 --> 00:03:53,767
[SALVADOR]<i> There are so many
</i> questions that needs answers.

75
00:03:53,967 --> 00:03:57,367
<i>after we interviewed
a woman whose husband,</i>

76
00:03:57,500 --> 00:03:59,133
<i> Rudy Magtibay,</i>

77
00:03:59,300 --> 00:04:00,667
<i>is currently in critical
condition at the hospital.</i>

78
00:04:00,833 --> 00:04:02,800
<i>After being shot
during this demolition,</i>

79
00:04:02,900 --> 00:04:05,367
<i>the public's questions
are heating up even more...</i>

80
00:04:05,500 --> 00:04:07,333
<i>why does someone
have to get hurt?</i>

81
00:04:07,733 --> 00:04:10,000
<i>In a demolition led
by the police,</i>

82
00:04:10,900 --> 00:04:14,633
<i>one question remains
in the family's mind,</i>

83
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:16,933
<i> who fired the shot?</i>

84
00:04:17,033 --> 00:04:19,000
<i> Who is to blame for this?</i>

85
00:04:19,867 --> 00:04:22,300
That Salvador is really
going too far.

86
00:04:22,667 --> 00:04:25,367
He won't stop until
he ruins NLEA.

87
00:04:25,500 --> 00:04:27,133
He's even working with them!

88
00:04:27,733 --> 00:04:29,233
[ESTRELLA] Ma'am,
if i'm being honest,

89
00:04:29,367 --> 00:04:32,033
what he said is true.

90
00:04:32,200 --> 00:04:33,500
What do you mean?

91
00:04:33,667 --> 00:04:34,667
[ESTRELLA] In the demolition,

92
00:04:34,767 --> 00:04:36,800
there was police
brutality involved.

93
00:04:38,033 --> 00:04:40,000
Severe police brutality!

94
00:04:40,100 --> 00:04:41,533
So you're saying...

95
00:04:41,700 --> 00:04:44,000
that we are the ones
who shot the victim?

96
00:04:44,167 --> 00:04:45,400
That's what I can't tell.

97
00:04:46,033 --> 00:04:47,367
But in my eyes,

98
00:04:48,067 --> 00:04:49,033
we overstepped.

99
00:04:49,533 --> 00:04:53,700
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

100
00:04:53,867 --> 00:04:55,367
[GROANS] Argh!

101
00:04:57,333 --> 00:04:59,667
[SALVADOR]<i> While the victim
</i> is fighting for their life,

102
00:04:59,833 --> 00:05:01,633
<i>his family is waiting
for an answer.</i>

103
00:05:01,767 --> 00:05:03,400
<i>- Who fired the shot?
- [MAX] Excuse me, sir.</i>

104
00:05:03,567 --> 00:05:05,700
- Yes?
- May I speak to you?

105
00:05:05,867 --> 00:05:08,100
Lieutenant Jacinto,
what is it about?

106
00:05:09,767 --> 00:05:12,500
About the excessive violence
during the demolition, sir.

107
00:05:12,967 --> 00:05:15,767
That would ruin the image
of the police.

108
00:05:15,900 --> 00:05:19,500
Someone could've died!
We overstepped, sir!

109
00:05:21,233 --> 00:05:22,533
Sit down, Lieutenant.

110
00:05:22,700 --> 00:05:28,433
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

111
00:05:28,567 --> 00:05:30,067
Before you scold me...

112
00:05:30,733 --> 00:05:35,867
and before you call me names,

113
00:05:38,067 --> 00:05:39,433
let's not forget

114
00:05:39,600 --> 00:05:43,533
who ordered the demolition
in Gininutang Lupa.

115
00:05:46,567 --> 00:05:47,867
it's your father, isn't it?

116
00:05:49,933 --> 00:05:51,900
Your father needs
to be held accountable.

117
00:05:52,000 --> 00:05:54,900
Your father is just
as responsible.

118
00:05:57,100 --> 00:05:58,067
Now.

119
00:05:58,633 --> 00:06:00,367
If you really love your father,

120
00:06:00,467 --> 00:06:02,200
and I believe you do.

121
00:06:04,067 --> 00:06:05,067
My advice?

122
00:06:05,767 --> 00:06:08,633
Shut up, Lieutenant Jacinto.

123
00:06:10,200 --> 00:06:11,500
Just shut up.

124
00:06:11,633 --> 00:06:19,467
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

125
00:06:22,533 --> 00:06:25,667
[TOTO] Sweetie! Sweetie!
Look at this!

126
00:06:25,800 --> 00:06:27,900
Please don't call me
Sweetie.

127
00:06:28,300 --> 00:06:30,767
- What's that?
- Here! Look!

128
00:06:31,200 --> 00:06:32,433
They just released it!

129
00:06:32,533 --> 00:06:35,567
[BETCHAY] We need your help!

130
00:06:35,667 --> 00:06:37,767
<i>We can't afford t
he medical bill!</i>

131
00:06:37,867 --> 00:06:39,633
[SALVADOR] While the victim
fights for his life,

132
00:06:39,800 --> 00:06:41,767
<i> his family waits for answers.</i>

133
00:06:41,900 --> 00:06:44,000
Who pulled the trigger, and why
<i> did what should have been</i>

134
00:06:44,167 --> 00:06:46,933
<i>an enforcement of the law
end in bloodshed?</i>

135
00:06:47,033 --> 00:06:49,100
We will never stop pursuing this

136
00:06:49,833 --> 00:06:52,300
<i>until whoever is responsible
is held accountable.</i>

137
00:06:52,400 --> 00:06:54,300
Oh no,
Sir needs to know about this!

138
00:06:54,400 --> 00:06:56,800
- Give it to me!
- Hey, hey, hey!

139
00:06:56,967 --> 00:06:59,367
Sweetie, stop right there!

140
00:06:59,500 --> 00:07:01,500
Let's not be stuck up!

141
00:07:01,667 --> 00:07:03,300
This is bad news!

142
00:07:03,400 --> 00:07:08,200
Who do you think they'll blame
when they watch that video?

143
00:07:08,333 --> 00:07:09,667
That's scary.

144
00:07:09,833 --> 00:07:12,300
It's a problem.
Why do we have to hide it?

145
00:07:12,400 --> 00:07:13,867
Don't you see?
This is bad news!

146
00:07:14,000 --> 00:07:16,133
We shouldn't be the ones
to tell them.

147
00:07:16,333 --> 00:07:20,167
Let them find out on their own.

148
00:07:28,367 --> 00:07:30,167
Four thousand.

149
00:07:30,267 --> 00:07:32,833
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC PLAYING]

150
00:07:32,933 --> 00:07:34,067
[SNIFFLES]

151
00:07:37,267 --> 00:07:39,167
[CRYING]

152
00:07:47,967 --> 00:07:49,667
What if...

153
00:07:51,967 --> 00:07:54,867
we don't get enough money
for Rudy's operation?

154
00:07:55,033 --> 00:07:59,500
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

155
00:07:59,600 --> 00:08:02,067
What if he dies? [CRYING]

156
00:08:07,800 --> 00:08:10,533
I can't handle it...
I don't think I can, Mameng!

157
00:08:10,633 --> 00:08:14,033
I don't think I can
handle losing him!

158
00:08:15,367 --> 00:08:17,333
He's the only man I ever loved!

159
00:08:18,467 --> 00:08:20,167
He's the only man I love!

160
00:08:21,400 --> 00:08:23,367
I don't think I can lose him!

161
00:08:24,600 --> 00:08:25,967
[MAMENG] Betchay...

162
00:08:26,500 --> 00:08:27,800
C'mon...

163
00:08:28,300 --> 00:08:29,800
don't be like that.

164
00:08:31,400 --> 00:08:34,233
Nothing bad will happen to Rudy.

165
00:08:34,967 --> 00:08:37,400
Gabo already has a job.

166
00:08:37,500 --> 00:08:41,033
He'll find a way!
We can save Rudy!

167
00:08:41,133 --> 00:08:42,733
It's always Gabo!

168
00:08:43,933 --> 00:08:47,133
It's always Gabo! Gabo! Gabo!

169
00:08:49,567 --> 00:08:54,267
I don't believe
that he can help us!

170
00:08:57,500 --> 00:08:59,233
C'mon, Mameng!

171
00:09:01,500 --> 00:09:03,167
He's your brother!

172
00:09:03,633 --> 00:09:05,233
He's your brother!

173
00:09:05,333 --> 00:09:09,800
He might die
if we don't get the money!

174
00:09:12,300 --> 00:09:14,400
Will anybody help us?!

175
00:09:16,667 --> 00:09:20,067
It's always me! It's always me!

176
00:09:22,467 --> 00:09:24,333
I'll find a way.

177
00:09:26,467 --> 00:09:28,267
I'll find a way.

178
00:09:29,833 --> 00:09:31,133
What will you do?

179
00:09:33,467 --> 00:09:34,933
Anything!

180
00:09:36,967 --> 00:09:40,300
I'll do anything to save Rudy.

181
00:09:42,567 --> 00:09:44,433
Even if I sell my own body!

182
00:09:46,467 --> 00:09:47,833
Betchay.

183
00:09:48,533 --> 00:09:50,300
[SIGHS]

184
00:09:50,400 --> 00:09:57,200
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

185
00:09:58,367 --> 00:10:00,133
[CRYING]

186
00:10:05,367 --> 00:10:11,633
[FOREBODING MUSIC PLAYING]

187
00:10:26,667 --> 00:10:28,767
[FOREBODING MUSIC CONTINUES]

188
00:10:28,767 --> 00:10:32,633
[DOOR CREAKS CLOSE]

189
00:10:49,600 --> 00:10:50,700
- Hey!
- Ooh!

190
00:10:50,700 --> 00:10:53,133
- Come drop by BeerGin!
- Hey, you, come visit!

191
00:10:53,133 --> 00:10:55,700
- We have a promo going on!
- Don't worry!

192
00:10:55,700 --> 00:10:57,467
[ROSANNA] The night is long.

193
00:10:57,467 --> 00:10:58,867
- [PRISCILLA GROANS]
- [JOYCE] Mm-hmm.

194
00:10:58,867 --> 00:10:59,933
- Just relax, girls.
- Hey, come in!

195
00:10:59,933 --> 00:11:01,567
- Oh, Betchay!
- Oh!

196
00:11:01,933 --> 00:11:03,200
How's Rudy doing?

197
00:11:03,200 --> 00:11:04,300
Uh...

198
00:11:04,300 --> 00:11:05,900
Was he able to get
an operation?

199
00:11:06,933 --> 00:11:09,100
Not yet. We still don't have
enough money

200
00:11:09,133 --> 00:11:11,133
so he's still unconscious.

201
00:11:11,133 --> 00:11:12,633
But is he doing alright?

202
00:11:13,300 --> 00:11:15,900
[SIGHS] He's in the ICU,
in critical condition.

203
00:11:15,900 --> 00:11:18,000
Oh, that's very unfortunate.

204
00:11:18,000 --> 00:11:19,133
Yeah...

205
00:11:19,133 --> 00:11:21,600
You know how hospitals work,
they're like taxis.

206
00:11:21,600 --> 00:11:23,100
It gets more expensive
as you go.

207
00:11:23,100 --> 00:11:26,533
Not to mention he's in the ICU
so the bills just get bigger.

208
00:11:27,267 --> 00:11:29,900
It isn't much but I hope
you accept this, Betchay.

209
00:11:29,900 --> 00:11:31,233
- Oh, really?
- Here, Betchay.

210
00:11:31,233 --> 00:11:33,333
- Oh, thank you, guys!
- It's not much, Betchay.

211
00:11:33,333 --> 00:11:35,500
Oh, I'm not going to say no
to these!

212
00:11:35,500 --> 00:11:37,467
Thank you so much to all of you!

213
00:11:38,133 --> 00:11:39,600
By the way, how are things
going here at the bar?

214
00:11:39,600 --> 00:11:41,400
Why? Are you doing a survey?

215
00:11:41,933 --> 00:11:44,300
Come on, I'm just asking.

216
00:11:44,300 --> 00:11:47,433
Oh, just ignore her. She's just
mad it's a slow day today.

217
00:11:48,000 --> 00:11:49,533
Our only customers right now

218
00:11:49,533 --> 00:11:51,500
are Boss Paquito
and his friends.

219
00:11:51,500 --> 00:11:53,100
[WHISPERING] Paquito's here?

220
00:11:53,100 --> 00:11:56,033
Perfect! I actually came here
to visit him.

221
00:11:56,033 --> 00:11:57,367
Are you gonna borrow money
from him?

222
00:11:57,367 --> 00:12:00,967
Oh, Betchay, you could get
in trouble

223
00:12:00,967 --> 00:12:02,400
because of what Gabo did.

224
00:12:02,600 --> 00:12:06,467
Screw it! He's the only one
who could give me what I need.

225
00:12:06,467 --> 00:12:07,700
A job!

226
00:12:07,700 --> 00:12:10,100
Come on, Betchay,
with that body of yours

227
00:12:10,100 --> 00:12:12,467
I don't think you can
break into a house anymore!

228
00:12:12,467 --> 00:12:14,433
Oh, not that!

229
00:12:15,167 --> 00:12:18,633
I was going to ask Paquito
if I could work here in BeerGin.

230
00:12:19,067 --> 00:12:21,333
Can you handle it? Will Rudy
even allow you to work

231
00:12:21,333 --> 00:12:22,200
as a hostess?

232
00:12:22,200 --> 00:12:24,533
Well, it used to be my job
anyway.

233
00:12:24,533 --> 00:12:25,533
Plus,

234
00:12:26,000 --> 00:12:28,167
I'm doing this for his sake.

235
00:12:28,967 --> 00:12:30,300
Alright, then.

236
00:12:30,300 --> 00:12:32,733
- Welcome. Head inside.
- Oh!

237
00:12:32,733 --> 00:12:33,867
- Hmm...
- Hey!

238
00:12:33,867 --> 00:12:36,033
[PAQUITO] But,
always keep this in mind,

239
00:12:36,033 --> 00:12:40,067
don't even try to fool me
because...

240
00:12:40,067 --> 00:12:41,333
you know me.

241
00:12:42,400 --> 00:12:44,533
We won't do shady business
behind you, Paquito.

242
00:12:44,533 --> 00:12:45,667
Nothing gets past you!

243
00:12:47,133 --> 00:12:49,400
- Well, then. Jack!
- Boss?

244
00:12:49,433 --> 00:12:50,767
Escort them out.

245
00:12:50,767 --> 00:12:52,633
Yes, boss. Follow me
this way, please.

246
00:12:53,433 --> 00:12:55,500
Boss, someone wants
to talk to you.

247
00:12:55,500 --> 00:12:57,267
Here comes the divas!

248
00:12:57,267 --> 00:12:59,767
[BETCHAY GIGGLING AWKWARDLY]
Hey, Paquito!

249
00:12:59,767 --> 00:13:02,233
Betchay, how can I help you?

250
00:13:02,667 --> 00:13:06,067
- I'm just wondering if--
- [ROSANNA] Boss!

251
00:13:06,067 --> 00:13:07,733
She's looking for a job.

252
00:13:07,733 --> 00:13:09,567
[ROSANNA] Take her in!
Come on!

253
00:13:10,600 --> 00:13:12,067
Oh, Betchay...

254
00:13:12,367 --> 00:13:15,267
your family committed
an offense against ours.

255
00:13:15,267 --> 00:13:18,167
How bold of you
to even come to me.

256
00:13:18,167 --> 00:13:19,567
Come on, Paquito.

257
00:13:19,567 --> 00:13:21,233
- Hm?
- Whatever happened

258
00:13:21,267 --> 00:13:23,400
between Gabo and Django
has nothing to do with me!

259
00:13:23,400 --> 00:13:26,100
- Huh?
- We're not related by blood!

260
00:13:26,100 --> 00:13:27,800
That's why we have different
personalities.

261
00:13:27,800 --> 00:13:29,400
- He's not right in the head
- Mm-hmm...

262
00:13:29,400 --> 00:13:31,333
but I am. Come on...

263
00:13:31,533 --> 00:13:34,000
The favor I'm asking for
isn't for Gabo's sake.

264
00:13:34,300 --> 00:13:35,767
[STUTTERING] I-- it's for me!

265
00:13:35,767 --> 00:13:38,133
Rudy just really needs it!

266
00:13:38,133 --> 00:13:39,700
- For his funeral!
- For the hospital!

267
00:13:39,700 --> 00:13:42,133
- Stop teasing, Paquito!
- [ROSANNA LAUGHING]

268
00:13:42,133 --> 00:13:44,800
Come on, I'm begging
on my knees here!

269
00:13:44,800 --> 00:13:46,633
- [PAQUITO LAUGHS]
- Just get her the job, man.

270
00:13:46,633 --> 00:13:48,367
She used to be a hostess
back in the day, right?

271
00:13:48,367 --> 00:13:50,133
But she's already
lost her touch!

272
00:13:50,133 --> 00:13:51,500
[ROSANNA] Oh, boss, you...

273
00:13:52,467 --> 00:13:54,100
Wait, you're right.

274
00:13:54,667 --> 00:13:56,333
Don't get cocky! You...

275
00:13:56,333 --> 00:13:59,133
Alright, alright.
I'll give you a chance.

276
00:13:59,333 --> 00:14:03,400
If someone books you tonight,
you're hired.

277
00:14:03,400 --> 00:14:05,267
[CLAPS] Thank you!

278
00:14:05,267 --> 00:14:07,167
- I'll give it my all! I swear!
- [PAQUITO LAUGHS]

279
00:14:07,167 --> 00:14:09,067
Oh, Betchay,

280
00:14:09,267 --> 00:14:11,467
if you don't secure a customer,

281
00:14:12,233 --> 00:14:14,233
you know what that means,
don't you?

282
00:14:14,233 --> 00:14:15,733
[PAQUITO LAUGHS]
Well then,

283
00:14:15,733 --> 00:14:17,767
- Osang, I'll leave her to you.
- Yes, boss.

284
00:14:17,767 --> 00:14:19,433
- Then, bye!
- Okay, boss!

285
00:14:19,433 --> 00:14:21,133
- Bye, divas!
- There.

286
00:14:21,133 --> 00:14:22,600
The boss took Betchay in.

287
00:14:22,600 --> 00:14:24,433
As if we aren't struggling
enough!

288
00:14:24,433 --> 00:14:25,733
- Leave her alone.
- Hmph!

289
00:14:25,733 --> 00:14:28,133
Betchay is in need right now!

290
00:14:28,167 --> 00:14:29,500
- [BETCHAY] Mm-hmm.
- That's right!

291
00:14:29,500 --> 00:14:31,100
Come on, stop acting
like a stranger!

292
00:14:31,100 --> 00:14:33,267
Aren't we all struggling here?

293
00:14:33,267 --> 00:14:34,800
Let's give and take!

294
00:14:34,800 --> 00:14:37,133
I'm not going to steal
your regulars from you.

295
00:14:37,133 --> 00:14:39,500
You won't be able
to snatch them away anyway.

296
00:14:39,500 --> 00:14:42,533
Okay, enough! The more,
the merrier, okay?

297
00:14:42,533 --> 00:14:44,700
Let's get to work!

298
00:14:44,700 --> 00:14:46,800
Don't mind these girls!

299
00:14:46,800 --> 00:14:49,533
Enough chatting! Go! Go!

300
00:14:49,533 --> 00:14:56,567
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

301
00:15:08,500 --> 00:15:09,567
Gentlemen!

302
00:15:09,567 --> 00:15:13,167
[FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING]

303
00:15:13,167 --> 00:15:14,367
Sir, I'll go with you!

304
00:15:15,467 --> 00:15:17,667
We have men doing
the collecting tonight, Colonel.

305
00:15:17,667 --> 00:15:20,800
Good. Business should
flow continuously.

306
00:15:20,800 --> 00:15:22,067
[UMALI] Sir, what's the matter?

307
00:15:22,067 --> 00:15:25,467
General, please-- Is there
something the matter?

308
00:15:25,467 --> 00:15:27,567
- General Duran--
- [THUDS]

309
00:15:27,567 --> 00:15:28,733
[GROANS, INHALES SHARPLY]

310
00:15:28,733 --> 00:15:31,333
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

311
00:15:31,333 --> 00:15:33,267
- Leave the room.
- No.

312
00:15:34,400 --> 00:15:36,833
I want your subordinates to hear

313
00:15:37,333 --> 00:15:39,200
just what kind of leader
you are.

314
00:15:39,200 --> 00:15:41,567
You've been keeping up
with the defamatory reports

315
00:15:41,567 --> 00:15:42,733
against us, I presume?

316
00:15:44,367 --> 00:15:45,767
I am, General. For now--

317
00:15:45,767 --> 00:15:47,600
- And you're just sitting here?!
- No, sir.

318
00:15:47,600 --> 00:15:49,900
- [THUDS]
- [GROANS, INHALES SHARPLY]

319
00:15:50,400 --> 00:15:52,167
- [DOMINGO GROANS]
- [GENERAL DURAN GRUNTS]

320
00:15:52,167 --> 00:15:54,900
You're letting our institution's
name get tarnished.

321
00:15:54,900 --> 00:15:56,933
No, I don't, General.
That's not true.

322
00:15:56,933 --> 00:16:00,733
The public is once again
wary against the police force.

323
00:16:01,233 --> 00:16:03,200
One wrong move

324
00:16:03,400 --> 00:16:04,667
and everyone suffers for it.

325
00:16:05,500 --> 00:16:09,733
Explain to me how things
got to this point.

326
00:16:09,767 --> 00:16:10,933
[INHALES SHARPLY]

327
00:16:11,300 --> 00:16:14,600
General Duran,
we did everything we could.

328
00:16:14,600 --> 00:16:17,800
We exercised maximum tolerance.
We followed the guidelines--

329
00:16:17,800 --> 00:16:19,600
But a civilian was shot!

330
00:16:21,933 --> 00:16:23,633
There's a story circulating

331
00:16:23,633 --> 00:16:26,233
to tarnish the image
of the police.

332
00:16:26,467 --> 00:16:27,467
[GENERAL DURAN SIGHS]

333
00:16:27,467 --> 00:16:30,167
- The truth is, General--
- The truth is...

334
00:16:30,633 --> 00:16:33,667
I don't think
you are a capable leader.

335
00:16:34,433 --> 00:16:35,533
[EXHLAES SHAKILY]

336
00:16:35,533 --> 00:16:37,933
I don't know how you'll fix this

337
00:16:37,933 --> 00:16:39,933
but you better fix it!

338
00:16:39,933 --> 00:16:46,933
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

339
00:16:57,567 --> 00:17:02,500
[CAR HORNS HONKING]

340
00:17:02,500 --> 00:17:05,867
[PRIEST]<i> To love and to cherish,
</i> till death do us part.

341
00:17:06,500 --> 00:17:09,567
May you all be filled with joy,
<i> and your hearts with love.</i>

342
00:17:09,567 --> 00:17:10,400
[PHONE CAMERA SHUTTER CLICKS]

343
00:17:10,400 --> 00:17:12,500
[TRADITIONAL CHINESE MUSIC
PLAYING]

344
00:17:12,500 --> 00:17:19,633
[GUESTS APPLAUDING]

345
00:17:22,800 --> 00:17:28,833
[FIREWORKS EXPLODING]

346
00:17:35,500 --> 00:17:37,267
[LAO] Boss,
thank you for coming.

347
00:17:37,267 --> 00:17:38,533
Thank you for coming.

348
00:17:38,533 --> 00:17:39,700
Thank you for coming, sir.

349
00:17:39,700 --> 00:17:41,533
- Where's your wife?
- Over there, sir.

350
00:17:41,533 --> 00:17:43,000
Still humoring her relatives.

351
00:17:43,000 --> 00:17:44,433
Norris.

352
00:17:45,533 --> 00:17:48,800
Give this to her. It's my gift.
Congratulations.

353
00:17:49,033 --> 00:17:50,800
Thank you, boss. Thank you.

354
00:17:51,033 --> 00:17:52,633
Now that you're wedded,

355
00:17:53,400 --> 00:17:54,733
you might lose your edge.

356
00:17:54,733 --> 00:17:56,600
Boss, that's impossible.

357
00:17:56,833 --> 00:17:59,567
I owe your brother a lot.

358
00:17:59,567 --> 00:18:01,800
I'll never leave
the group behind.

359
00:18:02,667 --> 00:18:04,733
Anyway. Boss, I'll just go back.

360
00:18:04,733 --> 00:18:08,333
- I'll just visit my wife.
- [PHONE RINGING]

361
00:18:09,733 --> 00:18:10,667
Hello, Ma?

362
00:18:10,667 --> 00:18:12,800
Are you on your way
to meet the buyer?

363
00:18:13,967 --> 00:18:17,333
Uh... I'm still at the wedding.

364
00:18:17,333 --> 00:18:19,433
Are we right on schedule?

365
00:18:19,633 --> 00:18:21,700
Why did you even
prioritize that?

366
00:18:21,700 --> 00:18:23,467
Okay. We'll be on our way.

367
00:18:23,833 --> 00:18:25,467
[PHONE BEEPING]

368
00:18:26,567 --> 00:18:28,433
- Stallone.
- Boss.

369
00:18:28,433 --> 00:18:30,600
Tell Lao we'll be on our way
to meet Mr. Chan.

370
00:18:30,600 --> 00:18:31,667
Yes, boss.

371
00:18:33,400 --> 00:18:34,867
[BREATHES SHARPLY]

372
00:18:34,867 --> 00:18:37,067
If this doesn't go smoothly...

373
00:18:39,900 --> 00:18:41,333
[DEBORAH SIGHS]

374
00:18:41,733 --> 00:18:45,833
You should've just let Lucas
take care of this.

375
00:18:45,833 --> 00:18:48,833
I told you, Lucas
is still not ready.

376
00:18:49,067 --> 00:18:51,333
Just trust Victor.

377
00:18:51,333 --> 00:18:52,933
He can manage all of this soon.

378
00:18:52,933 --> 00:18:59,433
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES, FADES]

379
00:18:59,467 --> 00:19:03,033
- [CAR HORN HONKS]
- [ENGINES REVVING]

380
00:19:03,033 --> 00:19:09,933
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

381
00:19:18,767 --> 00:19:19,867
[KAREN] It's getting late.

382
00:19:20,467 --> 00:19:22,400
Some stores are already closing

383
00:19:22,400 --> 00:19:24,567
and we still haven't gotten
a visual on Mr. Chan.

384
00:19:24,800 --> 00:19:26,667
[SEBASTIAN]<i> Sam,
</i> can you hear me?

385
00:19:26,933 --> 00:19:28,500
<i> What's your status over there?</i>

386
00:19:28,833 --> 00:19:30,600
Maybe the target already left.

387
00:19:31,667 --> 00:19:32,800
Don't worry.

388
00:19:33,000 --> 00:19:35,367
We're covering all possible
exit points.

389
00:19:38,467 --> 00:19:39,533
[IPE] Gabo.

390
00:19:39,767 --> 00:19:41,467
Is Mr. Chan really in there?

391
00:19:41,733 --> 00:19:43,867
What if we're just wasting
our time out here?

392
00:19:44,133 --> 00:19:45,633
Nothing we can do about it.

393
00:19:45,833 --> 00:19:46,967
This is my job.

394
00:19:47,467 --> 00:19:48,800
I need to find him.

395
00:19:49,667 --> 00:19:51,467
We'll just have to wait here...

396
00:19:51,933 --> 00:19:53,867
until we find Mr. Chan.

397
00:19:54,400 --> 00:19:56,067
Because he's the only one
who could tell us...

398
00:19:56,567 --> 00:19:57,900
who Tiger is.

399
00:19:57,900 --> 00:20:03,100
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

400
00:20:03,133 --> 00:20:07,500
[PHONE RINGING]

401
00:20:07,833 --> 00:20:09,133
Victor!

402
00:20:09,133 --> 00:20:10,700
[VICTOR] Mr. Chan!

403
00:20:10,700 --> 00:20:11,700
We're about to leave
the wedding.

404
00:20:11,700 --> 00:20:13,033
We're on our way to the bar.

405
00:20:13,033 --> 00:20:13,933
[MR. CHAN] Okay.

406
00:20:13,933 --> 00:20:15,967
- I'll see you. [JINGLING]
- Alright!

407
00:20:15,967 --> 00:20:17,500
One of my people, Lee,
is already there.

408
00:20:17,500 --> 00:20:18,767
She'll take care of you, okay?

409
00:20:18,767 --> 00:20:20,033
[MR. CHAN] Okay. Thank you.

410
00:20:20,033 --> 00:20:27,000
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC INTENSIFYING]

411
00:20:41,900 --> 00:20:43,800
Alright, here's the plan.

412
00:20:43,800 --> 00:20:47,833
I'll go inside and check if
Mr. Chan is still there.

413
00:20:47,833 --> 00:20:48,867
Okay. Be careful.

414
00:20:48,867 --> 00:20:55,833
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

415
00:20:56,867 --> 00:20:58,033
I have an idea.

416
00:20:58,033 --> 00:21:02,967
Tekla, go inside and find out
if Mr. Chan is in there.

417
00:21:02,967 --> 00:21:04,700
Hey, wait.

418
00:21:04,700 --> 00:21:06,933
I'm going there alone?
You're not coming with me?

419
00:21:08,133 --> 00:21:09,200
You can do it.

420
00:21:10,500 --> 00:21:12,500
It'd be better if you
go there alone.

421
00:21:12,500 --> 00:21:15,267
If we go as a group,
they might get suspicious

422
00:21:15,267 --> 00:21:17,233
and our plan could fail.

423
00:21:17,233 --> 00:21:18,500
Go.

424
00:21:18,500 --> 00:21:20,333
Alright. I'm going in.

425
00:21:21,833 --> 00:21:28,800
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

426
00:21:36,333 --> 00:21:43,867
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

427
00:21:47,033 --> 00:21:53,933
[OVERLAPPING CHATTER]

428
00:21:55,467 --> 00:21:58,000
- Hi!
- Hi!

429
00:21:58,800 --> 00:22:01,433
- Can I see this one?
- Sure.

430
00:22:01,433 --> 00:22:08,067
[THRILLING MUSIC PLAYING]

431
00:22:08,067 --> 00:22:10,100
- This is pretty.
- Mm-hmm.

432
00:22:10,100 --> 00:22:12,167
- How much is it?
- Let me check the price.

433
00:22:13,367 --> 00:22:16,133
Fifty-four thousand two
hundred forty pesos.

434
00:22:16,167 --> 00:22:17,967
Fifty-four thousand--
You see, miss...

435
00:22:17,967 --> 00:22:19,467
- I own a business.
- Oh.

436
00:22:19,467 --> 00:22:22,900
I was hoping to get a discount
if I buy in bulk.

437
00:22:22,900 --> 00:22:24,833
Can I talk to your boss?

438
00:22:24,833 --> 00:22:27,900
Oh, sure. I'll call Mr. Chan.
Just a sec.

439
00:22:27,900 --> 00:22:30,233
Shiela, can you please
assist her?

440
00:22:30,233 --> 00:22:32,133
- Hello, ma'am.
- Hello.

441
00:22:32,133 --> 00:22:35,400
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

442
00:22:35,400 --> 00:22:37,033
[SAM] Thank you.

443
00:22:38,900 --> 00:22:41,767
- [SAM] Can I see this one too?
- [SHIELA] Okay, ma'am.

444
00:22:43,333 --> 00:22:46,333
Wow! That's beautiful, miss!

445
00:22:46,333 --> 00:22:48,167
How much is this?
Does it look good on me?

446
00:22:48,200 --> 00:22:50,933
Excuse me.
That's reserved for me.

447
00:22:50,933 --> 00:22:52,467
- [QUIRKY MUSIC PLAYING]
- Oh, really?

448
00:22:52,467 --> 00:22:54,267
I don't see any name
on it.

449
00:22:54,267 --> 00:22:57,000
- How come it's reserved?
- I'm going to buy it.

450
00:22:57,000 --> 00:23:00,433
[SCOFFS] You're so cocky.

451
00:23:00,433 --> 00:23:02,167
What, you think you're pretty
and all that?

452
00:23:02,167 --> 00:23:05,500
Hey, you're just taller than me,
but I can compete with you.

453
00:23:05,500 --> 00:23:06,767
What?

454
00:23:08,167 --> 00:23:09,333
You know what, miss?

455
00:23:09,333 --> 00:23:11,467
If you'll just cause a scene,
you better stay away.

456
00:23:11,467 --> 00:23:13,933
[CHUCKLES] Don't talk to me
in English.

457
00:23:13,933 --> 00:23:15,533
We're not in America.

458
00:23:15,533 --> 00:23:18,867
And why are you wearing
a jacket? It's hot here.

459
00:23:18,867 --> 00:23:21,267
[STAFF] Miss, please don't
make a scene here.

460
00:23:21,267 --> 00:23:24,433
- I can kick you out of here.
- Yes, please. You do that.

461
00:23:24,467 --> 00:23:26,400
Hey! You're all arrogant!

462
00:23:26,400 --> 00:23:28,833
Stop acting all high
and mighty!

463
00:23:28,833 --> 00:23:30,900
- Call the security.
- How dare you?!

464
00:23:30,900 --> 00:23:32,533
- Guard! Guard!
- Call the guard.

465
00:23:32,533 --> 00:23:35,233
- She's causing a scene.
- No, I'm not!

466
00:23:35,233 --> 00:23:37,467
She started it! I was just
looking at jewelry!

467
00:23:37,467 --> 00:23:40,533
- Please go outside.
- No! I'm not causing a scene!

468
00:23:40,533 --> 00:23:43,400
- Take her outside.
- Don't touch me!

469
00:23:43,400 --> 00:23:46,500
- Where's the owner?! Hey!
- That's enough, ma'am.

470
00:23:46,500 --> 00:23:48,533
- [SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]
- Let's go.

471
00:23:48,533 --> 00:23:50,167
Faster, faster. Let's go.

472
00:23:50,167 --> 00:23:55,833
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

473
00:23:55,867 --> 00:23:59,533
- Just leave. Come on.
- I said let me go!

474
00:23:59,533 --> 00:24:02,667
Mr. Chan, there's someone
causing trouble here.

475
00:24:02,667 --> 00:24:04,433
- Who's that?
- A customer.

476
00:24:04,433 --> 00:24:06,100
Hey! I'm not causing
trouble, Mr. Chan!

477
00:24:06,100 --> 00:24:09,267
I'm a customer but they're
kicking me out!

478
00:24:09,267 --> 00:24:10,367
Get out! Get out!

479
00:24:10,367 --> 00:24:12,033
[TEKLA] You arrogant people!

480
00:24:12,033 --> 00:24:14,333
Hi, sir. I'm Carlota Diaz.

481
00:24:14,333 --> 00:24:19,200
I have an online business
and stalls in the province.

482
00:24:20,933 --> 00:24:22,467
Looks like Tekla got busted.

483
00:24:23,900 --> 00:24:25,000
[TEKLA] Ow!

484
00:24:25,000 --> 00:24:27,000
[SAM] I was thinking maybe
if I order in bulk,

485
00:24:27,000 --> 00:24:28,667
maybe you could give me
a discount?

486
00:24:28,700 --> 00:24:31,100
Okay. But not today.

487
00:24:31,100 --> 00:24:33,233
I have a meeting
at Jade Imperial.

488
00:24:34,200 --> 00:24:35,467
I'll give you my number.

489
00:24:35,467 --> 00:24:38,700
Call me tomorrow
or anytime, okay?

490
00:24:38,700 --> 00:24:39,600
[TEKLA] Hmph!

491
00:24:40,900 --> 00:24:41,967
I'll give you my card.

492
00:24:41,967 --> 00:24:45,433
We'll talk tomorrow or
next time. But not today.

493
00:24:45,433 --> 00:24:52,367
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

494
00:25:05,333 --> 00:25:06,400
- What happened?
- [TEKLA] Gabo!

495
00:25:06,567 --> 00:25:08,200
[SIGHS SHARPLY] There's this
pale-looking girl inside

496
00:25:08,333 --> 00:25:11,100
who acted like she's bought
the whole store.

497
00:25:11,833 --> 00:25:13,300
You started another fight?

498
00:25:13,433 --> 00:25:14,767
What about Gabo's task
for you?

499
00:25:14,900 --> 00:25:16,200
Yes, I started fight!

500
00:25:16,333 --> 00:25:18,633
But I only did that
to lure the owner out.

501
00:25:18,767 --> 00:25:19,867
- Ha!
- Then, what happened?

502
00:25:19,967 --> 00:25:22,533
It's confirmed!
It was Mr. Chan.

503
00:25:22,633 --> 00:25:24,100
I saw him with my own eyes.

504
00:25:24,233 --> 00:25:26,133
But I think he was
on his way out.

505
00:25:26,267 --> 00:25:28,467
He mentioned a
business meeting at...

506
00:25:29,800 --> 00:25:32,300
Jade... Jade Imperial?

507
00:25:35,400 --> 00:25:37,467
Team, the target
is on his way out.

508
00:25:39,667 --> 00:25:42,633
Visuals on target.
I repeat, visuals on target.

509
00:25:44,533 --> 00:25:47,567
Gabo! That's him!
Over there! That's Mr. Chan!

510
00:25:47,667 --> 00:25:48,667
In the red sunglasses!

511
00:25:48,800 --> 00:25:52,967
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

512
00:25:53,100 --> 00:25:54,567
Let's follow him.

513
00:25:57,833 --> 00:25:59,833
- Where's Daboy?
- He's at his post.

514
00:25:59,967 --> 00:26:02,000
Call him.
I'll just get my bike.

515
00:26:02,133 --> 00:26:03,900
I'll see you at Jade Imperial.

516
00:26:04,000 --> 00:26:05,833
- Go.
- [TEKLA] Okay.

517
00:26:05,967 --> 00:26:08,167
- I'll call him.
- Copy. See you later.

518
00:26:09,000 --> 00:26:10,700
[CELLPHONE RINGING]

519
00:26:10,833 --> 00:26:12,433
- Tekla.
- Hey, fart face!

520
00:26:12,567 --> 00:26:13,767
Where are you?

521
00:26:13,900 --> 00:26:16,333
"Fart face?"
We're at our post.

522
00:26:16,467 --> 00:26:18,833
Gabo's looking for you.
We found Mr. Chan.

523
00:26:18,967 --> 00:26:20,933
- We're going to follow him.
- [BUSY TONE]

524
00:26:21,033 --> 00:26:21,833
Where's Binoy?

525
00:26:21,967 --> 00:26:23,367
He went to take a piss
ages ago.

526
00:26:23,500 --> 00:26:25,267
Does he have a bladder problem?
Let's go get him.

527
00:26:25,367 --> 00:26:27,200
- Wait!
- Tekla called. Come on!

528
00:26:27,333 --> 00:26:28,433
Let's go.

529
00:26:28,533 --> 00:26:33,800
[ENGINE REVVING]

530
00:26:33,967 --> 00:26:38,467
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

531
00:26:38,633 --> 00:26:40,500
Follow Mr. Chan.
I'll be right behind you.

532
00:26:40,633 --> 00:26:41,533
Copy.

533
00:26:41,700 --> 00:26:42,567
Let's move!

534
00:26:47,000 --> 00:26:49,000
[ENGINE REVVING]

535
00:26:49,167 --> 00:26:56,067
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

536
00:27:12,333 --> 00:27:14,833
<i>I'll settle with the family
of the gunshot victim.</i>

537
00:27:15,000 --> 00:27:17,667
<i>They're in the wrong!
Now, they're whining online?!</i>

538
00:27:17,867 --> 00:27:20,333
<i>They won't stop. Looks like
they're demanding money.</i>

539
00:27:20,433 --> 00:27:21,600
<i> You need money, right?</i>

540
00:27:21,733 --> 00:27:24,200
<i>You know, Betchay, I've always
had my eyes on you.</i>

541
00:27:24,367 --> 00:27:26,733
<i>I've liked you
since we were kids.</i>

542
00:27:28,033 --> 00:27:29,900
The target is locked
on the enemy.

543
00:27:30,033 --> 00:27:31,333
[ENGINE ROARS]

544
00:27:32,367 --> 00:27:34,267
<i> If you see Tiger, alert us.</i>

545
00:27:34,400 --> 00:27:36,500
<i>- Why didn't you go inside?
- They require a... QT?</i>

546
00:27:36,633 --> 00:27:37,867
<i> It's QR! Stupid!</i>

547
00:27:38,033 --> 00:27:40,233
<i> We need to get in.</i>

548
00:27:43,267 --> 00:27:45,100
<i> Find a way to get inside.</i>

549
00:27:45,233 --> 00:27:47,600
The two groups
are in position,

550
00:27:47,733 --> 00:27:49,100
so this Thursday...

551
00:27:49,267 --> 00:27:51,700
<i>Looks like they're
a big-time syndicate.</i>

552
00:27:51,800 --> 00:27:54,733
<i>They're heavily armed, while
we're coming in empty-handed.</i>

553
00:27:54,900 --> 00:27:57,567
Brace yourselves for chaos.

554
00:27:57,733 --> 00:28:00,033
<i>NCIA! Hands in the air,
Victor Zafra!</i>

555
00:28:00,133 --> 00:28:01,467
[GUNSHOTS]

556
00:28:01,600 --> 00:28:03,100
[CLAMORING]

557
00:28:03,233 --> 00:28:04,600
- [ENGINE REVS]
- [TIRES SQUEAL]

558
00:28:05,667 --> 00:28:06,967
[BRAKES SCREECH]

559
00:28:07,100 --> 00:28:08,533
- [GUNSHOTS]
<i> - Follow them!</i>
